{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "TIT",
  "chapter": 3,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "TIT.3.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.3.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Put them in mind to be subject to principalities and powers, to obey magistrates, to be ready to every good work,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "TIT.3.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.3.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To speak evil of no man, to be no brawlers, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "but",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " gentle, showing all meekness to all men.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TIT.3.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.3.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For we ourselves also were sometimes foolish, disobedient, deceived, serving divers lusts and pleasures, living in malice and envy, hateful, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " hating one another.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TIT.3.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.3.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But when the kindness and love of God our Savior towards man appeared,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TIT.3.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.3.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Not by works of righteousness which we have done, but according to his mercy he saved us, by the washing of regeneration, and renewing of the Holy Spirit;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TIT.3.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.3.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Which he shed on us abundantly, through Jesus Christ our Savior;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TIT.3.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.3.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That being justified by his grace, we should be made heirs according to the hope of eternal life.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TIT.3.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.3.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "This is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a faithful saying, and these things I will that thou affirm constantly, that they who have believed in God may be careful to maintain good works. These things are good and profitable to men.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TIT.3.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.3.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But avoid foolish questions, and genealogies, and contentions, and strivings about the law; for they are unprofitable and vain.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TIT.3.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.3.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A man that is a heretic, after the first and second admonition, reject;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TIT.3.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.3.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Knowing that he who is such, is subverted, and sinneth, being condemned by himself.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TIT.3.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.3.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When I shall send Artemas to thee, or Tychicus, be diligent to come to me to Nicopolis: for I have determined there to winter.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TIT.3.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.3.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Bring Zenas the lawyer and Apollos on their journey diligently, that nothing may be wanting to them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TIT.3.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.3.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And let ours also learn to maintain good works for necessary uses, that they may not be unfruitful.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TIT.3.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.3.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "All that are with me salute thee. Greet them that love us in the faith. Grace ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with you all. Amen.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
